  "notes": "VERB TYPE:\n{自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive verb)\n\nIchidan verb ({一段動詞|いちだんどうし}/{上一段|かみいちだん})\n・{懲|こ}りない (negative)\n・{懲|こ}りて (te-form)\n・{懲|こ}りた (past)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・〜に{懲|こ}りる - to learn one's lesson from ~\n・{懲|こ}りずに - without learning one's lesson\n・{懲|こ}り{懲|ご}りする - to have absolutely had enough (emphatic)\n\nIDIOMATIC EXPRESSIONS:\n・{懲|こ}りない{人|ひと} - someone who never learns\n・{懲|こ}り{懲|ご}りだ - I've had more than enough\n\nUSAGE NOTES:\nOften used in the negative form {懲|こ}りない to describe someone who keeps making the same mistakes. The phrase {懲|こ}り{懲|ご}り is an emphatic form expressing complete exasperation.",
